IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cpf-self-employed`

-- Central Provident Fund Act 1953, ss 9A, 9(2)-(3), 9C, 13(4)(b), 13A, 58(1)(e), 61, 61B, 63 and 8A(9) with Fourth Schedule
-- paras 4-5 -- worked cases. Expected results written by hand.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. The regulations that hold the rate, the
-- income floor, the cap, the period and the interest rate were NOT retrieved; where an assertion needs one of those figures it
-- passes it in as an argument and says so.

§ `REQ-0268 (Jun Hao scenario, event j043)`

-- A self-employed delivery rider, born 30 August 2006 (aged 21 when he files on 18 April 2028), declares $31,000 of trade income
-- for a year. He is taken to be self-employed under the regulations, and the $31,000 to be assessable income from a trade (s 9A(3)),
-- NOT platform remuneration under s 8A(9). The Act imposes the duty:
#ASSERT `the receipt counts as income under section 9A(3)` TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `section 9A binds this income` TRUE FALSE FALSE

-- THE AMOUNT IS NOT IN THE ACT. STAND-IN, NOT LAW: 8% of income above a $6,000 floor, capped at $7,680. These are the CPF Board's
-- figures for a member under 35 with income over $18,000, as recalled by the encoder and NOT CHECKED against the regulations or a
-- Board publication. On those inputs: 8% of 31,000 = 2,480; under the cap.
#ASSERT `the section 9A contribution` 31000 0.08 6000 7680 EQUALS 2480

-- THE TIME IS NOT IN THE ACT either: "before the expiry of the prescribed period, or any longer period that the Board specifies".
-- With a stand-in prescribed period of 30 days and no extension, payment on day 30 is in time and on day 31 is overdue.
#ASSERT `the section 9A contribution is overdue` 30 30 0 EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the section 9A contribution is overdue` 31 30 0 EQUALS TRUE

-- If instead the $31,000 is remuneration from a delivery platform, paid on or after the s 8A(9) date, s 9A does not bind it; he is
-- a Group A platform worker (born on or after 1 January 1995), and the platform operator contributes under s 8A.
#ASSERT `section 9A binds this income` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the platform worker is a Group A worker` 2006 FALSE

§ `9A(3) -- income`

#ASSERT `the receipt counts as income under section 9A(3)` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the receipt counts as income under section 9A(3)` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the receipt counts as income under section 9A(3)` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

§ `9A(1), 8A(9) -- who is bound`

-- Not self-employed under the regulations: no duty.
#ASSERT `section 9A binds this income` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
-- Platform remuneration paid BEFORE the prescribed date stays under s 9A.
#ASSERT `section 9A binds this income` TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- The date passing does not matter for income that is not platform remuneration.
#ASSERT `section 9A binds this income` TRUE FALSE TRUE

§ `Fourth Schedule paras 4, 5 -- Group A`

#ASSERT `the platform worker is a Group A worker` 1995 FALSE
#ASSERT `the platform worker is a Group A worker` 1994 FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `the platform worker is a Group A worker` 1994 TRUE

§ `9A(1)(a) -- the amount, on stated inputs`

-- At or below the floor: nothing.
#ASSERT `the section 9A contribution` 6000 0.08 6000 7680 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the section 9A contribution` 5000 0.08 6000 7680 EQUALS 0
-- 4% of 10,000 = 400.
#ASSERT `the section 9A contribution` 10000 0.04 6000 7680 EQUALS 400
-- 8% of 120,000 = 9,600, capped at 7,680; 8% of 96,000 = 7,680 exactly.
#ASSERT `the section 9A contribution` 120000 0.08 6000 7680 EQUALS 7680
#ASSERT `the section 9A contribution` 96000 0.08 6000 7680 EQUALS 7680

§ `9C -- the Minister's waiver`

#ASSERT `the contribution payable after a section 9C waiver` 2480 480 EQUALS 2000
#ASSERT `the contribution payable after a section 9C waiver` 2480 3000 EQUALS 0

§ `9A(1)(b) -- the Board's longer period`

#ASSERT `the period for paying in days` 30 0 EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `the period for paying in days` 30 60 EQUALS 60
-- The Board can only lengthen it: a "shorter" figure is ignored.
#ASSERT `the period for paying in days` 30 20 EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `the section 9A contribution is overdue` 45 30 60 EQUALS FALSE

§ `9(2), (3) -- interest, on a stated daily rate`

-- 2,480 x 0.0005 x 10 days = 12.40.
#ASSERT `the interest under section 9(2)` 2480 0.0005 10 EQUALS 12.4
#ASSERT `the interest under section 9(2)` 2480 0.0005 0 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the interest payable after a section 9(3) waiver` 12.4 2.4 EQUALS 10

§ `58(1)(e), 61, 61B, 63 -- not paying`

#ASSERT `an offence under section 58(1)(e) is committed` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `an offence under section 58(1)(e) is committed` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `an offence under section 58(1)(e) is committed` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `an offence under section 58(1)(e) is committed` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS FALSE

#ASSERT `the maximum fine under section 61(1) in dollars` FALSE EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `the maximum fine under section 61(1) in dollars` TRUE EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `the maximum imprisonment under section 61(1) in months` FALSE EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `the maximum imprisonment under section 61(1) in months` TRUE EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `the minimum fine for a self-employed person's non-payment in dollars` EQUALS 0

-- 2,480 + 12.40 = 2,492.40.
#ASSERT `the most the court may order paid under section 61B(1)` 2480 12.4 EQUALS 2492.4
#ASSERT `the most the Board may collect to compound in dollars` TRUE EQUALS 1000
#ASSERT `the most the Board may collect to compound in dollars` FALSE EQUALS 0

§ `13(4)(b), 13A -- where the money goes`

#ASSERT `where a section 9A contribution is credited` FALSE EQUALS "the accounts the Minister directs under section 13(4)"
#ASSERT `where a section 9A contribution is credited` TRUE EQUALS "the medisave account"
#ASSERT `the licensing authority may make section 9A contributions a licence condition` TRUE
#ASSERT `the licensing authority may make section 9A contributions a licence condition` FALSE EQUALS FALSE
